/* ── Signature [scope-140] ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* nostromo's approved signature (Kenny, 2026-10-03, three review rounds): the
   progress bar and the ten elements (spinner, skeleton, switch, check and
   radio, toast, dialog, tooltip, wizard steps, empty state, link hover),
   ported once from research/progress-signature/themes/nostromo.css and research/signature-elements/themes/nostromo.css
   and maintained here from now on. In kp.signature, which css/themes.css
   orders after kp.register, so it draws over the register exactly as the
   approved demos did, whatever the weight of a register selector. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in nostromo's grammar: data pieces, empty-state drawings [kpadopt4] ──
   Nostromo's own (themes/nostromo/CHARACTER.md): the case is what you touch and the screen is what the ship reports
   (G7). A mark is a label plate (tape, 2 px, G6) with a lamp-lit pattern when it is a picture; a share bar is a lit
   window, its parts lit lenses and the free rest the unlit cells (G10's window); labels are tape, counts Michroma
   (G15); a changed reading lights its lamp (G9); a failed carrier sounds the klaxon (G13); a block of code or a command
   is a screen: amber phosphor on dark glass under scanlines, set in the plate's bezel (G7). Every drawing in an empty
   state is a vector written on such a screen, the raster's order, frame by frame (G2, G4). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in nostromo's grammar: pipeline, journey, moments, secret, dialog sections [kpadopt4] ──
   The pipeline is a rack: a lane a moulded plate, its head label tape with the stage's lit strip, a card a key with its
   lamp (G8): unlit at rest, lit under the hand, full when pressed, the LED orange on the open one; the board's words
   are a plate, a failed read the klaxon (G13). A journey is the LED bargraph laid between its steps: the way travelled
   lit in the step's own colour, the way to come unlit cells, a failed way alternate cells in red; the step it stands at
   is a lamp lit in its key. A moment on the timeline is a lamp, a stretch a run of lit cells (G10's window). The secret
   field is a screen: the value is written on it by the raster (G2) and the countdown is a bargraph that goes out cell by
   cell (G9, G10); a dialog's sections are divided by the vent seam and its danger section is framed all round (G13). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in nostromo's grammar: time, cooking and comparison [kpadopt4] ──
   Everything that reads a time out is the ship's screen: the digits of a countdown, a timer's remaining time and the
   timer disc are amber phosphor on dark glass in the case's bezel (G7, G15); an ended timer sounds the klaxon, framed
